# Line endings are part of this repository's test contract, not a preference.
#
# 80 of the 82 `apps/web/tests/db.*.test.ts` files -- plus ci.product-state,
# media.source-contract and r7-6-navigation-footer -- read a tracked file with
# readFileSync and assert `expect(text).toContain('multi\nline\nfragment')`.
# Those fragments are written with LF, so they can only match if the file on
# disk also uses LF.
#
# Every blob in this repository is already stored with LF. Without a
# .gitattributes, though, the *working tree* encoding is decided by whatever
# `core.autocrlf` the contributor happens to have: on a Windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` the files land as CRLF, every one of those assertions
# fails, and 14 tests break for a reason that has nothing to do with the code.
# CI runs on Linux and never sees it, so the suite is silently not reproducible
# off-Linux.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree instead of leaving it to local configuration.
# It changes no committed content -- the blobs are LF already.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
